Sharp Brain Gen1 built-in rescue initramfs
==========================================

The host BusyBox is an AArch64 dynamically linked binary and cannot execute
on the ARM926EJ-S target.  No ARMv5 static BusyBox source or binary was locally
available when this bring-up image was prepared, so this directory provides a
small GPL-2.0-only static rescue shell without requiring a network download.

Generate a deterministic newc archive (ordering, ownership and timestamps are
fixed):

  tools/brain-gen1-initramfs/build.sh /tmp/brain-gen1-initramfs.cpio

Then configure an out-of-tree kernel after loading brain_gen1_defconfig:

  scripts/config --file OUT/.config \
    --set-str INITRAMFS_SOURCE /tmp/brain-gen1-initramfs.cpio \
    --enable INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_NONE
  make O=OUT ARCH=arm CROSS_COMPILE=arm-linux-gnueabi- olddefconfig

The same static executable is installed as /init and /bin/sh.  PID 1 mounts
devtmpfs, proc, sysfs and devpts, then starts controlling-terminal rescue
shells on tty0 and ttyAMA0.  The tty0 shell accepts input from the Linux VT
keyboard path while the serial shell preserves recovery access.
